      "page_title": "AWS IAM",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "IAM helps you ==securely control access== to AWS services and resources."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Key Concepts"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "Users",
                "lines": [],
                "text": "Individual identity with permanent credentials",
                "icon": "iam"
              },
              {
                "title": "Groups",
                "lines": [],
                "text": "Collection of users; permissions assigned to groups",
                "icon": "iam"
              },
              {
                "title": "Roles",
                "lines": [],
                "text": "Identity you assume for temporary permissions",
                "icon": "iam"
              },
              {
                "title": "Policies",
                "lines": [],
                "text": "JSON documents defining permissions",
                "icon": "iam"
              },
              {
                "title": "Permissions",
                "lines": [],
                "text": "Allow or Deny access to resources",
                "icon": "iam"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Auth vs Authz"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "{blue:Authentication} = Who are you? (proving identity)",
            "{purple:Authorization} = What can you do? (access permissions)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "User",
              {
                "text": "Authentication",
                "sub": "Login",
                "ink": "blue"
              },
              {
                "text": "Authorization",
                "ink": "purple"
              },
              "AWS Resources"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Root User"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Created with the AWS account, has **full access**",
            "{red:Do not use} root for daily activities",
            "Enable MFA for the root user"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. MFA"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Adds an extra security layer, requires 2+ methods",
            "Virtual MFA (authenticator app)",
            "Hardware MFA (YubiKey)",
            "SMS MFA"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Least Privilege"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Principle",
          "text": "Grant only the ==minimum permissions== necessary to perform the job."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Reduces risk and improves security"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Policy Structure"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "json",
          "lines": [
            "{",
            "  \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",",
            "  \"Statement\": [{",
            "    \"Effect\": \"Allow\",",
            "    \"Action\": [\"s3:ListBucket\"],",
            "    \"Resource\": [\"arn:aws:s3:::my-bucket/*\"]",
            "  }]",
            "}"
          ],
          "note": "Effect, Action, Resource are required"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Policy Effect"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "{green:Allow} grants permission",
            "{red:Deny} explicitly blocks access"
          ]
        },
        {
